==[Module manifest]

The hand-written `catasto.ctmt` declaration.

A manifest is a catasto document: it declares `::kind(catasto, version: "1.0.0")`,
then the attributes of the `catasto` vocabulary it needs (shared Git repositories in
`::upstream(...)`, directory rules in `::zone(...)`), and maps workspace-relative paths
to constructor calls from the same vocabulary:

```text
`` ::kind(catasto, version: "1.0.0")
`` ::upstream(
``   vocabularies: catasto.git("https://example.com/vocabularies.git", rev: main, root: vocabularies)
`` )
``
`` "tmtroot/schema/writ.vocabulary.tmt": catasto.local("../vocabularies/writ.vocabulary.tmt")
``
`` "tmtroot/schema/rust.vocabulary.tmt": catasto.upstream(
``   vocabularies,
``   path: "rust/rust.vocabulary.tmt"
`` )
``
`` "scripts/deploy.sh": (
``   catasto.git("https://example.com/tools.git", rev: v1, path: "deploy.sh"),
``   executable: true
`` )
```

An upstream is resolved while the file is read, into the full `git`, `rev`
and `path` of \[`Source::Git`\] (joining `root` in front of `path`), so
everything after the parse, and the lockfile, see the same \[`Source`\]
either way.

===[Module url]

Git URL classification and validation.

====[Enums]

=====[enum UrlKind]

Where a repository lives, as far as catasto accepts it.

There is deliberately no ssh: `git@host:path`, `ssh://`, `git://` and plain
`http://` are rejected, so catasto never needs keys, agents or host config.

====[Functions]

=====[fn classify]

Classifies a `git` value from `catasto.ctmt`.

===[Functions]

====[fn vocabulary]

Returns the parsed canonical `catasto@1.0.0` vocabulary.

====[fn reject_misnamed]

Fails when `expected` is missing from `root` but a file whose name differs from it only in case is there.

The names catasto reads are exact. On a case-sensitive filesystem `Catasto.ctmt` would otherwise be read as
"no manifest" without a word, while on a case-insensitive one it would work, so one tree would behave
differently from one machine to the next.

====[fn is_inside_workspace]

===[Constants]

====[const MANIFEST_FILE]

File name of the manifest, relative to the workspace root.

====[const VOCABULARY_TMT]

Canonical `catasto@1.0.0` vocabulary source.

==[Module spec]

Manifest schema specifications for `catasto.ctmt`.

Provides \[`ConfigGroupSpec`\] representations of `::upstream` and manifest path entries
using `#[derive(Config)]` from `tomet-spec`.

===[Structs]

====[struct UpstreamSpec]

Upstream repository definitions declared in `::upstream(...)`.

An upstream declares a named `catasto.git(...)` repository at a pinned revision,
optionally with a `root` directory inside the repository from which entry paths start.

====[struct ManifestEntrySpec]

Manifest entry declaring a managed workspace file or repository.

Each top-level entry in `catasto.ctmt` binds a workspace-relative path
to a `catasto.{upstream,git,local,repo}(...)` constructor call; file entries
may optionally pair the call with `executable` in a tuple `(call, executable: bool)`.

====[struct ZoneSpec]

Directory schema rules declared in `::zone(...)`.

A zone maps a workspace-relative directory path pattern (using `<?...>` holes, or `"."` for
the workspace root) to constraints on child entries of each matching directory (and, when
`recursive: true`, its non-ignored subdirectories).

===[Functions]

====[fn all_manifest_specs]

Returns all configuration and declaration specification groups for `catasto.ctmt`.
